560
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:53,440
Monopoly is one of the top games of chance and strategy,

561
00:27:53,441 --> 00:27:56,440
and it begins with the roll of the dice.

562
00:27:56,441 --> 00:28:02,523
the dice. But the dice were around far before this iconic game was dreamt up.

563
00:28:02,524 --> 00:28:04,340
In fact, dice are among

564
00:28:04,341 --> 00:28:06,616
the oldest known gaming tools.

565
00:28:06,617 --> 00:28:11,320
In what's now southeastern Iran, they found a set of dice that

566
00:28:11,321 --> 00:28:16,862
dates back 3,000 years. The earliest known board games are even older.

567
00:28:16,863 --> 00:28:18,920
The Egyptians played board

568
00:28:18,921 --> 00:28:20,444
games 5,000 years ago.

569
00:28:20,445 --> 00:28:25,500
We don't know exactly what the rules of those games were, but other games

570
00:28:25,501 --> 00:28:28,460
from ancient times are still played today,

571
00:28:28,461 --> 00:28:31,540
and those include chess and Go.

572
00:28:31,541 --> 00:28:35,000
Go is possibly the world's oldest board game,

573
00:28:35,001 --> 00:28:37,580
still played in its original form,

574
00:28:37,581 --> 00:28:40,520
thought to have originated at least 2,500

575
00:28:40,521 --> 00:28:43,920
to 4,000 years ago in China.

576
00:28:43,921 --> 00:28:46,720
Some ancient board games aren't exactly the same

577
00:28:46,721 --> 00:28:48,480
as their modern versions.

578
00:28:48,481 --> 00:28:52,100
The earliest forms of chess were invented in India

579
00:28:52,101 --> 00:28:53,720
in the sixth century,

580
00:28:53,721 --> 00:28:57,780
And one specific military war game called Chaturanga

581
00:28:57,781 --> 00:29:02,640
was probably the one that most closely resembles modern-day chess.

582
00:29:03,020 --> 00:29:10,480
Our brains need to be reactivated in the way that chess allows you to activate your brain

583
00:29:10,481 --> 00:29:15,600
so that we are able to problem-solve the new problems that we are facing.

584
00:29:15,601 --> 00:29:22,380
We don't have all the algorithms, and chess allows us to strategize and figure things out.

585
00:29:22,381 --> 00:29:26,380
Some of these games have been around for thousands of years,

586
00:29:26,381 --> 00:29:30,380
and perhaps humans will be playing them for thousands of years to come.

587
00:29:35,380 --> 00:29:38,380
Some of our top toys and games are quite simple to design.

588
00:29:38,381 --> 00:29:46,380
What could be more basic than a box with a 25-watt bulb and some colorful plastic pegs?

589
00:29:47,380 --> 00:29:50,380
More than half a century after it was invented,

590
00:29:50,381 --> 00:29:55,380
Light Bright remains one of the most remembered and most loved toys.

591
00:29:57,380 --> 00:30:00,380
Light Bright was conceived in 1966,

592
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:04,380
when executives from a toy company were walking down Fifth Avenue in New York City

593
00:30:04,381 --> 00:30:09,380
and stopped to marvel at a window display made up of hundreds of colorful lights.

594
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:16,380
They set out to develop a toy that would allow children to create their own designs using light.

595
00:30:16,381 --> 00:30:18,920
But instead of hundreds of lights,

596
00:30:18,921 --> 00:30:21,260
their concept included a light box

597
00:30:21,261 --> 00:30:23,760
with a single low watt bulb

598
00:30:23,761 --> 00:30:25,760
with colorful plastic pegs

599
00:30:25,761 --> 00:30:29,260
that could be punched through a piece of black opaque paper.

600
00:30:29,261 --> 00:30:31,720
The prototype was pitched to Hasbro,

601
00:30:31,721 --> 00:30:33,660
who signed the deal within an hour.

602
00:30:33,661 --> 00:30:37,200
The first light bright sets hit the shelves in 1967

603
00:30:37,201 --> 00:30:41,700
with 400 plastic pegs and a variety of colors.

604
00:30:41,701 --> 00:30:45,780
The first sets were 9 inches wide and 12 inches high

605
00:30:45,781 --> 00:30:49,360
and came with templates for things like a boat, a train, and animals.

606
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:52,480
Later came numbers, letters, cartoon characters,

607
00:30:52,740 --> 00:30:56,800
but the real appeal was the ability to unleash the imagination

608
00:30:56,801 --> 00:31:00,400
and create almost any picture with light.

609
00:31:00,401 --> 00:31:04,680
And 54 years after the first Lifebride sets hit the shelves,

610
00:31:05,100 --> 00:31:07,840
this nostalgic classic is still loved today.

611
00:31:08,220 --> 00:31:10,480
And sometimes bigger is definitely better,

612
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:15,740
like gigantic light boards that fill kids and adults alike with wonder.

613
00:31:15,780 --> 00:31:18,820
and artists who use the same basic technology

614
00:31:18,920 --> 00:31:21,780
to create amazing works of art.

615
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:25,320
Playing Monopoly is not all chance.

