619
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:34,940
whether it's a battle on the high seas,

620
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:36,740
solving a murder mystery,

621
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:40,440
or even plotting for world domination.

622
00:31:40,540 --> 00:31:44,140
In the early 1950s, the famous French film director

623
00:31:44,141 --> 00:31:49,140
Albert Lamourisse invented a board game called La Conquête du Monde,

624
00:31:49,141 --> 00:31:53,140
which translates to Conquest of the World.

625
00:31:53,141 --> 00:31:57,140
And the game was introduced to the US in 1959.

626
00:31:57,141 --> 00:32:01,140
But it went by a different name, Risk.

627
00:32:01,141 --> 00:32:07,140
More than 100,000 units of the game sold in its first year.

628
00:32:07,141 --> 00:32:13,140
Another game of strategy that centers on warfare has origins that are less clear.

629
00:32:13,141 --> 00:32:18,140
It's been said that Battleship was invented early in the 20th century,

630
00:32:18,141 --> 00:32:22,140
enjoyed by soldiers of World War I, and played with pen and paper.

631
00:32:22,141 --> 00:32:28,140
Today, between video game apps and electronic versions of the Milton Bradley game,

632
00:32:28,141 --> 00:32:32,140
they've sold over 100 million units.

633
00:32:34,140 --> 00:32:39,140
And strategy games aren't set entirely within military context.

634
00:32:39,141 --> 00:32:44,140
One of the most well-known games of strategy may be Clue.

635
00:32:44,141 --> 00:32:48,140
The game was released in 1949 and was invented by musician

636
00:32:48,141 --> 00:32:51,140
